/-!
# `row_residue` for q = 6 through `ZMod 17`

`vSeedPrime 6 = 17`.  Data (all checked exactly in Python, see `checks/`):
* `q6rzD r` is the lcm of the denominators of row `r` of
  `q6SourceMatrixAtZeroExplicit`; `q6rzN0 = diag(q6rzD) * M_0` and
  `q6rzAN = diag(q6rzD) * A` are integer matrices, so
  `diag(q6rzD) * M_t = q6rzN0 - t * q6rzAN`;
* for `t = 0..4`, `q6rzE * q6rzNbar_t = q6rzL_t * q6rzU_t` in `ZMod 17`, with
  `q6rzE` upper and `q6rzL_t` lower unitriangular, and `q6rzNbar_t` the residue of
  `q6rzN0 - t * q6rzAN`;
* `q6rzW` inverts the Vandermonde matrix `(tʲ)` modulo 17.

No rational determinant at `T ≠ 0`, no rational interpolation, and no 9 by 9
Leibniz expansion occurs.  Every `decide` acts on entries below 17, on one
`ℤ → ZMod 17` cast, on one 9-term dot product, or on the product of nine
small naturals.  Determinants are reached only through `Matrix.det_mul`,
`Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular`/`isLowerTriangular` and `RingHom.map_det`.
Exact coefficient residues: [5, 12, 4, 7, 4] = `vSeedResidueRow 6`.
-/

namespace Li2Lean.B3

noncomputable section

open Li2Lean
open Matrix

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 20000000

instance q6rzFact : Fact (Nat.Prime (vSeedPrime 6)) := ⟨by norm_num [vSeedPrime]⟩

